All such polynomials are exactly the following:
- P(X) = 0;
- P(X) = 1;
- P(X) = (X − 1)^2;
- P(X) = X(X − 1)⋯(X − k) for some nonnegative integer k;
- P(X) = X(X − 1)⋯(X − k) (X − k − 2)^2 for some nonnegative integer k.

Exactly the distributions where every box has either 12, 25, 38, 51, or 64 balls, with the counts satisfying t + 2u + 3v + 4w = 4 (where t, u, v, w are the numbers of boxes with 25, 38, 51, 64 balls respectively) and all remaining boxes have 12 balls. Concretely, the five possibilities are:
- 78 boxes with 12 balls and 1 box with 64 balls;
- 77 boxes with 12 balls, 1 box with 51 balls, and 1 box with 25 balls;
- 77 boxes with 12 balls and 2 boxes with 38 balls;
- 76 boxes with 12 balls, 1 box with 38 balls, and 2 boxes with 25 balls;
- 75 boxes with 12 balls and 4 boxes with 25 balls.
